    "summary": "Adire cloth: woman&#039;s: composed of two even lengths of machine plain woven European cotton machine sewn together. The textile is decorated using the starch resist method. The producer has applied the starch through stencils before dyeing the textile indigo. The designs represent two umbrellas, two standing figures, and a seated crowned King. The pattern is divided into 12 regular oblongs in 4 rows of 3 and is repeated six times on each half of the cloth. The hems are machine sewn and signed by the producer.",
